After reviewing `src/libs/ReportUtils.ts`, the function `isLastAdmin` is not suitable as it only checks for the last *admin* of a policy expense chat. I need a function that checks for the last *member* of any room.

I will add a new function `isLastMember` to `ReportUtils.ts`. This function will take a `report` object as input and return `true` if the current user is the last member of the room.

Here's the implementation of `isLastMember`:

```typescript
function isLastMember(report: OnyxEntry<Report>, personalDetails: OnyxEntry<PersonalDetailsList>): boolean {
    if (!report || !report.participants) {
        return false;
    }

    const participants = Object.keys(report.participants);
    if (participants.length !== 1) {
        return false;
    }

    const lastMemberAccountID = Number(participants[0]);
    return lastMemberAccountID === SessionUtils.getAccountID();
}
```
Now, I will add this function to `src/libs/ReportUtils.ts`. I will also need to import `SessionUtils`. After that, I will modify the `leaveRoom` function.
I'll begin by adding `isLastMember` to `ReportUtils.ts`.

